WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:03.350
<b>Tomozaki</b>

00:04.400 --> 00:07.230
<b><i>"You thought I meant I liked 
you </i>that<i> way, didn't you!"</i></b>

00:07.570 --> 00:09.820
<b><i>"I actually do like you that way."</i></b>

00:11.110 --> 00:14.450
<b><i>Who, a bottom-tier character like me?</i></b>

00:14.890 --> 00:17.390
<b><i>This calls for some top-tier assistance.</i></b>

00:18.370 --> 00:23.250
<b>Aoi Hinami</b>

00:19.760 --> 00:22.370
<b><i>I guess I'll have to go 
to Hinami for advice...</i></b>

00:22.370 --> 00:23.250
<b>Takehiro Mizusawa: Sorry, Fumiya. Can 
you come to work? Someone called in sick.</b>

00:24.250 --> 00:28.000
<b>Takehiro Mizusawa: Sorry, Fumiya. Can 
you come to work? Someone called in sick.</b>

00:25.530 --> 00:26.780
<b><i>Mizusawa?</i></b>

02:01.850 --> 02:06.930
<b>2nd Stage: Lv. 9 
If you don't make up your mind,
the story won't advance</b>

02:02.090 --> 02:04.070
<b>Sorry for the short notice.</b>

02:04.070 --> 02:05.620
<b>This is a big help.</b>

02:05.620 --> 02:06.530
<b>Sure.</b>

02:07.330 --> 02:08.600
<b>What's wrong, Fumiya?</b>

02:09.330 --> 02:12.980
<b><i>It's not like I can tell him about Mimimi.</i></b>

02:13.450 --> 02:16.990
<b>Aha! Girl trouble, perhaps?</b>

02:18.340 --> 02:20.080
<b>Hey, I got it right.</b>

02:20.080 --> 02:24.660
<b>So were you dumped? Did you jump 
the gun on confessing your love?</b>

02:25.010 --> 02:27.660
<b>Dumped? No, not dumped...</b>

02:28.950 --> 02:31.160
<b>Oh? Then did someone open up to <i>you</i>?</b>

02:31.160 --> 02:34.710
<b>You've been spending a lot of 
time alone with Kikuchi lately.</b>

02:34.990 --> 02:36.840
<b>Huh? Kikuchi?</b>

02:37.950 --> 02:39.220
<b>No?</b>

02:39.460 --> 02:41.600
<b>Uh... no...</b>

02:42.340 --> 02:44.910
<b>Hmm... Then that means...</b>

02:45.510 --> 02:47.520
<b>the other possibility would be...</b>

02:49.030 --> 02:50.190
<b>Mimimi?</b>

02:51.730 --> 02:55.070
<b>Whoa, seriously? Mimimi?</b>

02:56.180 --> 02:57.320
<b>Hmm.</b>

02:57.760 --> 02:59.290
<b>I see.</b>

03:00.010 --> 03:02.450
<b>So what's got you confused?</b>

03:02.770 --> 03:07.470
<b>I don't even know if it counts 
as a confession, for one.</b>

03:07.940 --> 03:09.830
<b>It's hard to say.</b>

03:10.160 --> 03:13.830
<b>Could be a confession, or 
she could be playing games.</b>

03:14.640 --> 03:16.340
<b>Games...</b>

03:16.610 --> 03:19.280
<b>If you want to continue the 
relationship you've had so far,</b>

03:19.280 --> 03:23.350
<b>you can totally go on 
as if nothing happened.</b>

03:23.350 --> 03:25.580
<b>I-I can, huh?</b>

03:25.580 --> 03:27.930
<b>Although I <i>would</i> say that...</b>

03:27.930 --> 03:33.310
<b>if you wanted to date her in this 
situation, you can probably do that, too.</b>

03:33.310 --> 03:34.020
<b>What?!</b>

03:34.020 --> 03:35.520
<b>Keep it down!</b>

03:36.710 --> 03:38.150
<b>S-Sorry...</b>

03:38.480 --> 03:42.980
<b>But yeah, I can see why 
she'd be feeling the heat.</b>

03:42.980 --> 03:44.400
<b>What's that mean?</b>

03:44.400 --> 03:47.660
<b>Remember? Attractive guys attract people.</b>

03:48.000 --> 03:55.180
<b>Mimimi's probably fretting about 
you getting snapped up by Kikuchi</b>

03:55.180 --> 03:57.420
<b>or someone at the girls' school.</b>

03:57.810 --> 04:00.620
<b>Y-Yeah, but even if I did get snapped up,</b>

04:00.620 --> 04:02.300
<b>there are plenty of other options...</b>

04:02.570 --> 04:03.550
<b>Listen.</b>

04:04.690 --> 04:07.390
<b>When are you going to quit 
with that masochistic crap?</b>

04:07.830 --> 04:10.980
<b>You're just wielding your 
weakness as an excuse</b>

04:10.980 --> 04:14.140
<b>so you don't have to acknowledge 
anyone's expectations or goodwill,</b>

04:14.450 --> 04:15.950
<b>and it's a <i>terrible habit</i>.</b>

04:16.710 --> 04:18.210
<b>Haven't you noticed?</b>

04:18.210 --> 04:23.030
<b>Whenever you're putting yourself 
down, you look almost relieved.</b>

04:24.410 --> 04:26.260
<b>Don't do that.</b>

04:27.040 --> 04:30.630
<b>A <i>truly</i> cool guy is only relieved</b>

04:30.630 --> 04:35.320
<b>after raising the bar for himself, 
then eagerly putting in the work</b>

04:35.320 --> 04:37.320
<b>to be able to clear it.</b>

04:38.100 --> 04:42.220
<b>I mean, honestly, you're free 
to keep denigrating yourself.</b>

04:42.220 --> 04:43.420
<b>I don't care either way.</b>

04:43.680 --> 04:46.930
<b>But when you put yourself down,</b>

04:47.200 --> 04:51.040
<b>it upsets the people who like you.</b>

04:59.360 --> 05:04.360
<b><i>I guess I </i>am<i> an undisputed bottom-tier 
character in this game called life.</i></b>

05:04.900 --> 05:09.840
<b><i>I go on about truth and sincerity while 
using my own weakness as an excuse,</i></b>

05:09.840 --> 05:13.590
<b><i>shutting down my thoughts with "No one 
would ever choose the likes of me."</i></b>

05:13.590 --> 05:18.130
<b><i>But maybe I knew that, somewhere deep down.</i></b>

05:18.600 --> 05:21.320
<b><i>Maybe I was just pretending not to notice.</i></b>

05:21.910 --> 05:26.720
<b><i>Which is exactly why I'm 
going to voice <i>this</i> truth</i></b>

05:26.720 --> 05:28.970
<b><i>in the realest sense of the word:</i></b>

05:29.680 --> 05:33.520
<b><i>Yes, Minami Nanami...</i></b>

05:34.970 --> 05:37.660
<b><i>She... she likes me.</i></b>

05:38.980 --> 05:41.230
<b>Sewing Room 2</b>

05:40.490 --> 05:41.230
<b>Now then,</b>

05:41.230 --> 05:44.690
<b>Today's Task: Decide who you want to get closer to</b>

05:41.620 --> 05:47.240
<b>you've chosen your two or 
more girls to pursue, yes?</b>

05:44.690 --> 05:47.240
<b>Small Goal: Who do you want to get closer to?</b>

05:47.470 --> 05:50.240
<b>Can I ask you something, Hinami?</b>

05:50.240 --> 05:51.240
<b>What?</b>

05:51.480 --> 05:55.700
<b>What does it mean to... to fall for someone?</b>

05:56.340 --> 05:59.080
<b>How can you ask something so 
embarrassing with a straight face?</b>

05:59.690 --> 06:03.960
<b>S-Stop it. I was doing fine 
till you said something.</b>

06:04.860 --> 06:07.440
<b>Well, if we look at it analytically...</b>

06:07.440 --> 06:13.350
<b>It's when reliance, lust, possessiveness, 
and interest coincide.</b>

06:13.350 --> 06:16.850
<b>Precisely speaking, it would be an emotion</b>

06:17.500 --> 06:19.360
<b>made up of a combination of these factors.</b>

06:19.360 --> 06:23.900
<b>No, I mean in a more individual way.</b>

06:23.900 --> 06:27.490
<b>Something like... who do I like?</b>

06:27.490 --> 06:31.740
<b>How do I even know how to tell?</b>

06:33.200 --> 06:34.990
<b>Are you still going on about that?</b>

06:35.280 --> 06:38.120
<b>I do <i>want</i> to make up my mind,</b>

06:38.120 --> 06:41.380
<b>but I can't yet. Or something.</b>

06:41.600 --> 06:46.160
<b>See, this is why you need to 
choose two or more people.</b>

06:46.160 --> 06:51.390
<b>You honestly can't decide, yet you're 
compelled to narrow it down to just one.</b>

06:51.930 --> 06:55.010
<b>Isn't that much more insincere?</b>

06:56.900 --> 07:02.400
<b>Or perhaps there's not a single 
girl you're vaguely interested in?</b>

07:02.680 --> 07:05.650
<b>No... that's not it...</b>

07:05.950 --> 07:09.630
<b>I'm not telling you to run out 
there and declare your love.</b>

07:09.630 --> 07:11.550
<b>You don't even have to be certain about it.</b>

07:12.030 --> 07:17.160
<b>Just decide who you'd like to become 
closer to from now on. That's all.</b>

07:12.780 --> 07:17.160
<b>Small Goal: Who do you want to get closer to?</b>

07:19.160 --> 07:20.140
<b>Got it.</b>

07:21.260 --> 07:22.970
<b>The girls I'm interested in</b>

07:24.950 --> 07:26.670
<b>are Mimimi and Kikuchi.</b>

07:29.760 --> 07:35.850
<b>An extremely appropriate answer, given 
all your hesitation. What a letdown.</b>

07:32.340 --> 07:35.850
<b>Small Goal: CLEAR! 
Who do you want to get closer to? 
Mimimi / Kikuchi</b>

07:36.410 --> 07:37.850
<b>Oh, hush.</b>

07:38.360 --> 07:40.850
<b>Okay, so starting today,</b>

07:40.850 --> 07:43.830
<b>you'll get closer to them 
on the premise of building</b>

07:43.830 --> 07:45.860
<b>a boyfriend-girlfriend relationship.</b>

07:46.160 --> 07:48.360
<b>Boyfriend... girlfriend...</b>

07:48.610 --> 07:50.530
<b>Picture this:</b>

07:50.530 --> 07:52.610
<b>Mimimi comes to your room,</b>

07:53.100 --> 07:55.700
<b><i>and the two of you sit on your bed, alone.</i></b>

07:55.700 --> 07:57.950
<b><i>A lot of words are exchanged,</i></b>

07:57.950 --> 08:00.200
<b><i>your fingers are entwined...</i></b>

08:01.000 --> 08:03.040
<b><i>Or you're with Fuka,</i></b>

08:03.040 --> 08:05.290
<b><i>and a lot of words are exchanged,</i></b>

08:05.580 --> 08:07.790
<b><i>your fingers are entwined...</i></b>

08:09.320 --> 08:10.420
<b>Okay!</b>

08:11.050 --> 08:13.300
<b>Looks like you got it.</b>

08:13.620 --> 08:14.990
<b><i>Damn her...</i></b>

08:15.790 --> 08:18.810
<b>Now, first up, your new goal:</b>

08:18.810 --> 08:21.810
<b>New Goal: Decide which one you like</b>

08:19.340 --> 08:21.810
<b>Decide which one you like.</b>

08:22.440 --> 08:24.060
<b>Once you have that answer,</b>

08:24.060 --> 08:27.000
<b>work on conveying your feelings to her.</b>

08:27.640 --> 08:29.920
<b>Your small goal will be...</b>

08:27.650 --> 08:34.990
<b>Small Goal: Complete event map (before culture festival)</b>

08:29.920 --> 08:34.990
<b>to complete a normie romance event 
map before the culture festival.</b>

08:35.290 --> 08:37.370
<b>An event map?</b>

08:37.370 --> 08:42.450
<b>Minami Nanami Route 
- Event 1 
 - Event 2 
- Event 3 
Fuka Kikuchi Route  
- Event 1 
 - Event 2 
- Event 3</b>

08:38.040 --> 08:42.450
<b>Like in a dating sim?</b>

08:43.010 --> 08:44.190
<b><i>Hex</i>actly!</b>

08:45.120 --> 08:48.710
<b>And if you ultimately confess your 
feelings to her and start dating,</b>

08:48.710 --> 08:51.840
<b>Medium Goal: Have a girlfriend 
before starting year 3</b>

08:49.290 --> 08:51.320
<b>you'll have met your medium goal.</b>

08:52.240 --> 08:53.590
<b>Now hang on a second...</b>

08:53.590 --> 08:55.140
<b>What is it?</b>

08:55.140 --> 08:58.460
<b>I don't want to make confession a goal.</b>

08:58.460 --> 09:00.600
<b>If I'm going to tell a girl how I feel,</b>

09:00.600 --> 09:04.140
<b>it can't be for some goal or task...</b>

09:05.670 --> 09:10.360
<b>it's got to be because I, 
myself, <i>want</i> to tell her.</b>

09:10.650 --> 09:14.310
<b>What? Are you saying that the 
<i>process</i> is what matters here,</b>

09:14.310 --> 09:17.110
<b>regardless of the outcome?</b>

09:17.440 --> 09:19.120
<b><i>nanashi</i> is saying this?</b>

09:19.400 --> 09:23.250
<b>I do think the outcome is important, too.</b>

09:23.250 --> 09:25.750
<b>Right? Then who cares?</b>

09:26.010 --> 09:30.760
<b>nanashi's play style is all about valuing 
both the process and the result.</b>

09:30.760 --> 09:33.760
<b>That's how I got to be 
Japan's top-ranked player.</b>

09:33.760 --> 09:34.760
<b>I mean,</b>

09:35.340 --> 09:39.810
<b>it's got to be more efficient to 
fight that way IRL, too, right?</b>

09:40.890 --> 09:44.810
<b>Well, if you insist, I guess, sure.</b>

09:45.660 --> 09:49.440
<b>Okay, next we'll go into more 
detail on the event map.</b>

09:46.810 --> 09:50.310
<b>Small Goal: Complete event map (before culture festival)</b>

09:49.440 --> 09:50.310
<b>Right.</b>

09:50.310 --> 09:54.320
<b>I've just sent you three 
events you'll need to clear.</b>

09:56.400 --> 09:58.320
<b>First up:</b>

09:58.320 --> 10:01.830
<b>Discuss what you're looking for in a dating partner</b>

09:58.830 --> 10:01.830
<b>Discuss what you're looking 
for in a dating partner.</b>

10:02.160 --> 10:04.330
<b>Th-That's pretty direct...</b>

10:04.610 --> 10:05.580
<b>Second:</b>

10:05.580 --> 10:09.580
<b>Touch each others' hands on purpose for at least 5 seconds straight</b>

10:05.580 --> 10:09.580
<b>Touch each others' hands <i>on purpose </i>
for at least 5 seconds straight.</b>

10:09.830 --> 10:11.080
<b>Wh-What?!</b>

10:11.490 --> 10:12.340
<b>Third:</b>

10:12.340 --> 10:15.840
<b>Wear matching accessories just for you two</b>

10:12.860 --> 10:15.840
<b>Wear matching accessories, just for you two.</b>

10:15.840 --> 10:21.850
<b>Wait wait wait! 
Aren't these all incredibly hard?!</b>

10:22.140 --> 10:25.490
<b>They are. But you can do it.</b>

10:25.490 --> 10:26.380
<b>Eh?</b>

10:26.380 --> 10:30.860
<b>After all, you've managed to 
complete almost every task so far.</b>

10:31.440 --> 10:32.510
<b>Isn't that right?</b>

10:46.100 --> 10:47.000
<b>Here goes.</b>

10:50.130 --> 10:53.910
<b>This new cheese curry on 
the school lunch menu...</b>

10:53.910 --> 10:56.720
<b>pulling some strings as 
student council prez, I see!</b>

10:56.720 --> 10:58.590
<b>Who, me? No way!</b>

10:58.590 --> 11:00.330
<b>Are you <i>sure</i>?</b>

11:09.560 --> 11:11.910
<b><i>Wh-What's going on?</i></b>

11:11.910 --> 11:13.620
<b>What's wrong, Mimimi?</b>

11:14.400 --> 11:19.740
<b><i>Damn. Now Hinami will see that 
Mimimi's acting weird, too.</i></b>

11:27.210 --> 11:31.540
<b><i>Mizusawa said we could always 
just carry on as we always had,</i></b>

11:32.390 --> 11:33.970
<b><i>but that's looking unlikely.</i></b>

11:34.790 --> 11:37.800
<b>Did something happen with Mimimi? 
Nothing in particular</b>

11:39.800 --> 11:43.300
<b>Ah. Well, as long as you're getting 
through those tasks of yours</b>

11:50.770 --> 11:55.440
<b><i>First, what we're looking for in a partner...</i></b>

11:52.190 --> 11:55.440
<b>Discuss what you're looking for in a dating partner</b>

11:56.480 --> 11:57.770
<b>Sorry I'm late.</b>

11:57.770 --> 11:59.050
<b>Whoa!</b>

11:59.780 --> 12:01.400
<b>I-I'm sorry.</b>

12:01.400 --> 12:03.660
<b>Did I startle you?</b>

12:03.900 --> 12:06.760
<b>Oh, no... you're fine.</b>

12:07.410 --> 12:10.410
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly 
First Draft</b>

12:08.940 --> 12:10.410
<b>Oh, wow!</b>

12:10.820 --> 12:12.550
<b>It's like a real script!</b>

12:13.710 --> 12:15.190
<b>Isn't it?</b>

12:15.190 --> 12:18.300
<b>That was fast, though. You're done already?</b>

12:18.570 --> 12:23.620
<b>Um, I still haven't figured 
out the second half.</b>

12:23.620 --> 12:25.600
<b>Oh, no?</b>

12:25.600 --> 12:28.180
<b>But it's kind of fun, somehow.</b>

12:29.100 --> 12:34.290
<b>I get so excited when I picture these 
characters coming to life on stage.</b>

12:34.980 --> 12:37.520
<b>And a little nervous, too.</b>

12:37.520 --> 12:39.090
<b>I get it.</b>

12:39.680 --> 12:43.340
<b>All those people watching 
the festival stage...</b>

12:44.660 --> 12:47.570
<b>Okay, I'll give this a read-through</b>

12:48.010 --> 12:50.080
<b>and we'll met up again after school.</b>

12:50.410 --> 12:52.110
<b>Thanks in advance.</b>

12:52.700 --> 12:54.620
<b>Oh, um, a-actually...</b>

12:55.010 --> 12:56.950
<b>Yes? What is it?</b>

12:56.950 --> 12:59.220
<b>Well, uh...</b>

13:00.000 --> 13:01.340
<b>What's wrong?</b>

13:03.260 --> 13:04.840
<b>Discuss what you're looking for in a dating partner</b>

13:04.840 --> 13:07.100
<b><i></i>Now<i> what do I do?</i></b>

13:09.660 --> 13:12.220
<b><i>I know! If Fuka's my choice...</i></b>

13:13.120 --> 13:17.050
<b>Earlier you said you were 
trying to figure out</b>

13:17.050 --> 13:21.610
<b>who the hero Libra would wind 
up with at the climax, right?</b>

13:21.940 --> 13:25.610
<b>Right. Kris or Alucia.</b>

13:25.930 --> 13:29.120
<b>People who see romance as a 
matter of who winds up with who</b>

13:29.570 --> 13:32.070
<b>are going to be really 
invested in this story.</b>

13:32.070 --> 13:32.920
<b>Uh-huh.</b>

13:33.450 --> 13:40.400
<b>So, um... if a guy and 
a girl are g-going out,</b>

13:40.400 --> 13:42.880
<b>what do <i>you</i> think their criteria should be?</b>

13:43.160 --> 13:46.720
<b>Their criteria for choosing someone to date?</b>

13:46.720 --> 13:49.140
<b>Y-Yeah. Right.</b>

13:50.670 --> 13:55.140
<b>There's still so much I don't know...</b>

13:55.820 --> 13:59.400
<b>But I think it probably depends on</b>

13:59.850 --> 14:03.900
<b>what "dating" means to any given person.</b>

14:05.070 --> 14:07.320
<b>What it means?</b>

14:07.860 --> 14:12.950
<b>If someone is simply interested 
in trying this "dating" thing,</b>

14:12.950 --> 14:17.580
<b>or if a couple wants to put a name 
on the relationship they share...</b>

14:18.890 --> 14:20.210
<b>I see.</b>

14:20.880 --> 14:24.550
<b><i>That probably counts for my task, anyway...</i></b>

14:21.590 --> 14:24.550
<b>Discuss what you're looking for in a dating partner</b>

14:24.850 --> 14:28.000
<b><i>But I'd like to take it a step further.</i></b>

14:29.280 --> 14:36.560
<b>O-Okay, then, what does "dating" 
mean for you personally?</b>

14:37.180 --> 14:40.060
<b>Me? Personally?</b>

14:40.350 --> 14:41.820
<b>Uh-huh.</b>

14:42.310 --> 14:43.520
<b>Um...</b>

14:43.930 --> 14:49.160
<b>Well, there's this Andi story, 
"The Scissorman's Lie."</b>

14:49.160 --> 14:53.910
<b>Oh, that one. The short love story 
about the Scissorman and the princess.</b>

14:53.910 --> 14:54.830
<b>Right.</b>

14:54.830 --> 15:04.340
<b>The Scissorman's Lie</b>

14:55.680 --> 15:00.630
<b>A man with scissors for hands who 
hurts people without meaning to</b>

15:00.630 --> 15:04.340
<b>gets pulled into a storybook world 
and falls in love with a princess.</b>

15:05.030 --> 15:08.910
<b>A bond gradually grows 
between the lonely pair.</b>

15:09.830 --> 15:13.440
<b>The Scissorman is the only 
one for the princess,</b>

15:13.440 --> 15:17.300
<b>and the princess is the only 
one for the Scissorman.</b>

15:18.660 --> 15:24.150
<b>I think dating might mean being able 
to create that kind of relationship.</b>

15:24.990 --> 15:28.700
<b>Where no one else could 
take your partner's place.</b>

15:29.120 --> 15:30.350
<b>That's right.</b>

15:30.350 --> 15:37.790
<b>A special relationship, where no one 
else will do, taking one ideal shape.</b>

15:38.090 --> 15:43.290
<b>I think that might be what 
"dating" means to me.</b>

15:44.170 --> 15:46.980
<b>One ideal shape, huh?</b>

15:46.980 --> 15:49.550
<b>I'll have to give that some thought myself.</b>

15:49.890 --> 15:52.800
<b>You don't have a take on it?</b>

15:53.400 --> 15:56.490
<b>Mmm... I never really thought about it.</b>

15:56.490 --> 15:58.150
<b>Oh, I see.</b>

15:58.150 --> 16:05.560
<b>But that's all the more reason I ought to 
pin down my own definition of "dating."</b>

16:05.840 --> 16:11.070
<b>Well, once you do, 
please share it with me.</b>

16:12.700 --> 16:18.330
<b>Oh! To, um... to help with 
the script, that is...</b>

16:18.590 --> 16:20.950
<b>A-As reference.</b>

16:20.950 --> 16:23.460
<b>Right. As reference.</b>

16:28.840 --> 16:30.720
<b>Yo, Fumiya.</b>

16:30.720 --> 16:32.470
<b>What's up, Mizusawa?</b>

16:34.520 --> 16:36.470
<b>Sure is awkward between you and Mimimi.</b>

16:36.470 --> 16:38.190
<b>Oh, well...</b>

16:38.780 --> 16:40.080
<b>you know...</b>

16:40.080 --> 16:42.510
<b>This calls for drastic measures.</b>

16:43.670 --> 16:44.980
<b>Let's get to lunch.</b>

16:44.980 --> 16:45.770
<b>Huh?</b>

16:47.020 --> 16:49.020
<b>Bottom-Tier Character Tomozaki S2</b>

16:53.820 --> 16:56.320
<b>Oh! Mapo bowl for you, Brain?</b>

16:56.630 --> 16:58.830
<b>A-And ramen for you, Mimimi?</b>

17:01.810 --> 17:03.280
<b>Hey, Tomozaki?</b>

17:03.280 --> 17:04.830
<b>Y-Yeah?</b>

17:05.340 --> 17:08.590
<b>About... About yesterday...</b>

17:10.720 --> 17:14.000
<b>I mean, don't worry about it too much.</b>

17:14.000 --> 17:15.550
<b>In fact, forget it!</b>

17:16.250 --> 17:19.000
<b>Or, well, not exactly.</b>

17:19.000 --> 17:22.810
<b>Let's just be like we always 
have been... or something.</b>

17:23.080 --> 17:24.810
<b>S-Sure.</b>

17:24.810 --> 17:26.050
<b>Got it.</b>

17:28.480 --> 17:30.860
<b>Huh! Who knew?</b>

17:30.860 --> 17:32.610
<b>Same goes for you, right, Aoi?</b>

17:32.610 --> 17:34.030
<b>That's right!</b>

17:34.030 --> 17:38.110
<b>I've had people ask if you 
and I are dating, Takahiro!</b>

17:39.250 --> 17:44.400
<b>Oh, yeah, those two would 
make a <i>great</i> couple.</b>

17:44.400 --> 17:46.330
<b>If you <i>do</i> say so yourself.</b>

17:46.840 --> 17:49.460
<b>Actually, Tomozaki... what about <i>you</i>?</b>

17:51.720 --> 17:53.710
<b>Um...</b>

17:53.950 --> 17:58.070
<b><i>I can feel her pressing me to 
make the most of this setting</i></b>

17:58.070 --> 17:59.720
<b><i>to get my tasks over with.</i></b>

17:59.970 --> 18:01.600
<b>M-Me?</b>

18:01.600 --> 18:06.370
<b>Yeah! It's like you seem to have 
something going on, but you don't...</b>

18:06.370 --> 18:08.610
<b>or it seems like you <i>don't</i>, but you <i>do</i>.</b>

18:08.610 --> 18:09.980
<b><i>Well, which is it?</i></b>

18:09.980 --> 18:15.240
<b>Oh, he might. He was at that girls' school 
culture festival, after all.</b>

18:15.700 --> 18:18.240
<b>Talking to girls and everything.</b>

18:20.120 --> 18:23.620
<b>I wouldn't be surprised if 
something developed after that.</b>

18:24.020 --> 18:26.120
<b>I-Is that true, Brain?!</b>

18:26.120 --> 18:28.960
<b>N-No, there's nothing!</b>

18:29.690 --> 18:31.020
<b>Hmm...</b>

18:31.020 --> 18:32.820
<b>You know, Minmi...</b>

18:32.820 --> 18:34.400
<b>Wh-What?</b>

18:34.400 --> 18:35.800
<b>You're weird today.</b>

18:35.800 --> 18:39.120
<b>Oh, that? I thought so, too.</b>

18:39.120 --> 18:42.300
<b>I bet she's hiding something from us!</b>

18:42.640 --> 18:46.140
<b>I-I wouldn't... say <i>that</i>...</b>

18:46.140 --> 18:50.400
<b><i>Whoa, Mimimi—this is </i>not<i> the 
time to be looking my way!</i></b>

18:50.720 --> 18:54.320
<b>Now, now. Setting that aside...</b>

18:54.320 --> 18:57.400
<b>Whoops—my ramen's gonna get soggy!</b>

18:57.400 --> 19:00.610
<b>Everyone eat up fast before it gets cold!</b>

19:04.910 --> 19:06.910
<b>My Unfamiliar Way to Fly</b>

19:07.850 --> 19:12.580
<b><i>"My Unfamiliar Way to Fly" went like this:</i></b>

19:13.720 --> 19:16.490
<b><i>In a world where dragons 
and humans lived in harmony,</i></b>

19:16.490 --> 19:21.000
<b><i>there was one very special 
breed of flying dragon.</i></b>

19:21.000 --> 19:24.300
<b><i>Susceptible to stress and wary of humans,</i></b>

19:24.300 --> 19:27.450
<b><i>the most important factor in raising them was</i></b>

19:27.450 --> 19:30.520
<b><i>never exposing them to the 
impurities of the world.</i></b>

19:31.580 --> 19:37.540
<b><i>Libra, the locksmith's son, and Alucia, 
next in line to be queen, were both 15.</i></b>

19:37.540 --> 19:39.770
<b><i>They grew up together, despite 
their different backgrounds.</i></b>

19:40.320 --> 19:44.580
<b><i>When Libra was younger, he visited the 
castle on an errand for his father,</i></b>

19:44.580 --> 19:47.170
<b><i>where he met the smart and determined Alucia,</i></b>

19:47.170 --> 19:48.610
<b><i>and the two became friends.</i></b>

19:49.790 --> 19:53.040
<b><i>One day, while his father was working,</i></b>

19:53.040 --> 19:57.330
<b><i>Alucia invited Libra to explore the castle.</i></b>

19:58.540 --> 20:03.100
<b><i>Inside it was a garden they 
were forbidden to enter.</i></b>

20:03.100 --> 20:06.750
<b><i>Out of curiosity, the two went in.</i></b>

20:07.500 --> 20:12.930
<b><i>There before them was a pure-white 
dragon with huge wings</i></b>

20:12.930 --> 20:16.670
<b><i>and Kris, a young girl who knew 
nothing of the outside world.</i></b>

20:17.580 --> 20:22.230
<b><i>Kris had been abandoned 
outside the castle as a baby,</i></b>

20:22.230 --> 20:24.720
<b><i>and was also 15 years old.</i></b>

20:24.720 --> 20:29.150
<b><i>She lived here, apart from the world, 
to serve as the dragon keeper.</i></b>

20:30.000 --> 20:32.700
<b><i>Neither she nor the dragons 
were permitted to have contact</i></b>

20:32.700 --> 20:34.980
<b><i>with any humans who weren't royalty.</i></b>

20:37.370 --> 20:42.950
<b><i>The king sentenced Libra to death for 
having entered the forbidden garden.</i></b>

20:43.850 --> 20:48.940
<b><i>But Alucia confronted her father, 
the king, with a hard truth:</i></b>

20:49.830 --> 20:54.600
<b><i>the king had illegitimate children 
hidden throughout the kingdom.</i></b>

20:55.110 --> 20:58.960
<b><i>Alucia bluffed that Libra 
was one of these children,</i></b>

20:58.960 --> 21:03.610
<b><i>making him royalty—and her brother.</i></b>

21:04.720 --> 21:09.320
<b><i>And if Libra were royalty, he 
couldn't contaminate the dragons.</i></b>

21:10.350 --> 21:14.210
<b><i>Not wanting his dirty little 
secret to go public,</i></b>

21:14.210 --> 21:16.550
<b><i>the king vacated Libra's sentence,</i></b>

21:17.570 --> 21:22.670
<b><i>and Libra was charged with caring for Kris.</i></b>

21:25.650 --> 21:26.780
<b>Um...</b>

21:27.700 --> 21:29.010
<b>I enjoyed it.</b>

21:29.010 --> 21:31.140
<b>Y-You did? Really?!</b>

21:31.450 --> 21:36.640
<b>Uh-huh. It felt a lot like the way 
it did when I read the story itself.</b>

21:36.940 --> 21:38.650
<b>Thank goodness...</b>

21:39.000 --> 21:43.900
<b>Um, w-would you say you 
had any concerns so far?</b>

21:44.470 --> 21:45.820
<b>Hmm...</b>

21:46.290 --> 21:47.780
<b>Maybe the characters?</b>

21:48.480 --> 21:49.900
<b>The characters?</b>

21:50.880 --> 21:53.820
<b>They feel... more <i>ordinary</i> now, or something.</b>

21:53.820 --> 21:56.910
<b>I'm sure the story is easier 
to understand this way,</b>

21:56.910 --> 21:59.920
<b>but it's like there's 
something off about them.</b>

22:00.170 --> 22:02.170
<b>Maybe so...</b>

22:02.770 --> 22:06.070
<b>I actually did change the concept a little.</b>

22:06.070 --> 22:11.550
<b>I simplified the characters to make it 
easier for everyone to play the various parts.</b>

22:11.840 --> 22:16.850
<b>But in making them easier to understand, 
they may have become more broadly drawn.</b>

22:17.760 --> 22:18.850
<b>Ah, I see.</b>

22:19.450 --> 22:24.190
<b><i>Her short stories are strong on portraying 
the characters' fine details,</i></b>

22:24.190 --> 22:26.940
<b><i>the particular ways they think, 
even their inconsistent feelings.</i></b>

22:27.200 --> 22:30.200
<b>That was a big part of its charm.</b>

22:30.540 --> 22:32.550
<b>I thought I'd do without complex emotions</b>

22:32.550 --> 22:35.580
<b>and bring straightforward 
thoughts to the forefront.</b>

22:37.300 --> 22:40.280
<b>But I feel like that weakened 
the sense I had before</b>

22:40.280 --> 22:43.070
<b>that these were living, 
breathing characters.</b>

22:43.680 --> 22:47.590
<b>Can I keep on writing this as is?</b>

22:48.360 --> 22:53.220
<b>I... I think you should go 
back the original characters.</b>

22:55.610 --> 22:58.100
<b>It might make them harder to perform,</b>

22:58.600 --> 23:03.230
<b>and it might be hard for you to 
get that across in just dialogue.</b>

23:04.070 --> 23:04.720
<b>But...</b>

23:05.560 --> 23:08.240
<b>I think that way is absolutely 
more interesting.</b>

23:10.360 --> 23:13.740
<b>All right, understood. I'll give it a try.</b>

23:16.910 --> 23:19.500
<b><i></i>Way<i> too much happened today.</i></b>

23:19.800 --> 23:21.630
<b><i>I feel like my head's going to pop.</i></b>

23:22.500 --> 23:25.000
<b><i>What should I be thinking about?</i></b>

23:25.000 --> 23:26.870
<b><i>What should I do?</i></b>

23:27.790 --> 23:29.510
<b><i>What does "dating" mean?</i></b>

23:29.990 --> 23:32.510
<b><i>And if I ever find out...</i></b>

23:32.910 --> 23:35.100
<b><i>who will I most want to be with,</i></b>

23:35.600 --> 23:38.780
<b><i>Mimimi or Kikuchi?</i></b>
